.TH FSPROTO 2
.SH NAME
fsproto: ReadFile, ReadString \- read filesystem prototypes in Ziran
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
Proto :: #import "fsproto";
Files :: #import "fsproto_files";

result: Proto.ProtoResult
ok := Proto.ReadFile(path, root, *result)
ok = Proto.ReadString(text, root, *result)

count := Proto.ItemCount(*result)
old_path := Proto.ItemOldPath(*result, index)
new_path := Proto.ItemNewPath(*result, index)
dir: Files.DirEntry
Proto.ItemDir(*result, index, *dir)

count = Proto.DiagCount(*result)
level := Proto.DiagLevel(*result, index)
line := Proto.DiagLine(*result, index)
path := Proto.DiagPath(*result, index)
message := Proto.DiagMsg(*result, index)
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fsproto
reads filesystem prototype files as defined by
.IR proto (6).
The module is part of the TaijiOS Ziran SDK.
Bind the
.B taijios_io
host interface when building a guest bundle.
.PP
.B ReadFile
reads a prototype from a guest file.
.B ReadString
reads prototype text supplied by the caller.
Both traverse the filesystem rooted at
.I root
and replace the entries and diagnostics in
.IR result .
They return false if opening or reading the prototype fails, or if a fatal
prototype error stops traversal. Recoverable warnings leave the return value
true and remain in the diagnostics.
.PP
Entries preserve traversal order. Each holds its source path, destination
path and owned directory metadata. Source paths follow the prototype's
explicit or inherited source names. Destination paths begin with a slash
and describe names under the destination root.
.B ItemOldPath
and
.B ItemNewPath
return owned Text values.
.B ItemDir
copies the metadata into the caller's
.BR Files.DirEntry .
That record includes name, owner, group, modifier, mode, access and modification
times, length and identity.
.PP
The parser preserves single-quoted names and doubled single quotes,
$environment substitutions (with $user read from /dev/user), octal modes with
directory, append and exclusive flags, indentation, and inherited source paths.
Wildcard + expands directories recursively, * lists their immediate entries,
and % lists immediate files. Wildcard entries are sorted by name.
As in the original reader, owner and group fields in the prototype are parsed;
returned ownership comes from the source metadata.
.PP
Diagnostics own their source path and message, and include the prototype line
number and severity. Severity is
.B Proto.WARN
for recoverable problems and
.B Proto.FATAL
when traversal stops. Entries collected before a fatal error remain available.
Missing files skip their indented children. No background walker or completion
channel is required: the result is complete when the read returns.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/lib/fsproto.zi
.br
.B /appl/lib/fsproto_files.zi
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR fs (1),
.IR proto (6),
.IR mkfs (8)
